NUBEBAR LICENCE

Copyright (c) 2026 P542-X. All rights reserved.

NubeBar is free of charge. It is not open source: the code is visible so you can
read it and check what it does to your machine — the least you can ask of a
program that replaces your taskbar — but its author keeps the rights to it.

YOU MAY
  1. USE it, free of charge, on as many machines as you like, at home or at
     work, without paying and without asking.
  2. COPY AND SHARE it as it comes, at no charge. If you pass it on, pass this
     licence on with it.
  3. READ the source, study it, and build it for yourself.

YOU MAY NOT
  4. SELL it: not the program, not a copy of it, not inside a paid product,
     bundle or service. No charging for installing or distributing it either.
  5. MODIFY IT OR PUBLISH CHANGED VERSIONS. You may build it and tinker with it
     on your own machine; what you may not do is distribute the result, publish
     a modified version, a derivative work, or a changed fork.
  6. REMOVE THE ATTRIBUTION. The name, the copyright notices and this licence
     travel with the program.

NO WARRANTY
  The program is provided AS IS, without warranty of any kind. The author is not
  liable for any damage, data loss or trouble arising from its use. NubeBar
  hides the Windows taskbar while it runs: although it ships a watchdog that
  gives it back if something goes wrong, you use it at your own risk.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
  This licence covers NubeBar's own code. Third-party components keep their own
  licences (listed above), which are more permissive than this one, and you may
  keep using those components under their own terms.

For any other use — selling, modifying, redistributing with changes, including
it in another product — written permission from the author is required. Ask by
opening an issue at github.com/P542-X/NubeBar.
